<title>FRANCE: Lagardere falls on Apache report.</title>
<headline>Lagardere falls on Apache report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lagardere shares fell on Tuesday after a newspaper reported that Germany would not buy the air-launched Apache cruise missile for its Tornado jets.</p>
<p>Groupe Lagardere's Matra Defense Espace subsidiary is prime contractor on the Apache missile, with state-owned SNI Aerospatiale as a subcontractor.</p>
<p>Financial daily Les Echos reported that the head of Germany's BWB arms procurement office has written to his French counterpart that the German air force will not buy the air-launched version of the missile, which is designed to crater enemy runways.</p>
<p>The share was off 2.75 percent at 124 francs at 1042 GMT, while the CAC-40 index was off 0.24 percent.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
